ui-radio-buttons-are-often-arranged-in-stacked-layouts-list-them-vertically-with-an-appropria = Radio buttons are often arranged in stacked layouts. List them vertically with an appropriate option preselected. Use an adjacent label for every option; short, distinct labels are easier to scan.

ui-adjacent-label-text = Adjacent label text

ui-always-pair-a-radio-button-with-a-label-describing-what-it-selects-each-choice-needs-its-o = Always pair a radio button with a label describing what it selects. Each choice needs its own label. The label and the radio select the same option; label text keeps the on surface color during interaction.

ui-selecting-a-radio-button-deselects-the-previous-option-activating-the-selected-option-does = Selecting a radio button deselects the previous option. Activating the selected option does not clear it. A group can start with a selection or with no selection, but should provide a suitable default whenever possible.

ui-apply-a-settings-change-immediately-when-appropriate-in-a-form-or-dialog-keep-a-draft-sele = Apply a settings change immediately when appropriate. In a form or dialog, keep a draft selection until the person confirms. Cancel restores the saved value; Continue commits the selected language in this example.

ui-people-using-assistive-technology-should-be-able-to-navigate-to-a-radio-button-select-a-ra = People using assistive technology should be able to:
    • Navigate to a radio button
    • Select a radio button
    • Get appropriate feedback for the input type

ui-a-radio-button-can-be-selected-or-unselected-selecting-one-deselects-the-others-a-group-ma = A radio button can be selected or unselected. Selecting one deselects the others. A group may start with one selection or none. Once an option is selected, selecting it again doesn't clear it.

ui-to-let-people-opt-out-provide-a-not-applicable-or-no-option-choice-or-a-separate-clear-sel = To let people opt out, provide a Not applicable or No option choice, or a separate Clear selection action. People must be able to select either the radio or its text label.

ui-keep-targets-at-least-48-48dp-by-default-let-people-explicitly-choose-a-denser-layout-or-t = Keep targets at least 48 × 48dp by default. Let people explicitly choose a denser layout or theme. Keep the controls that reverse a density setting at least 48 × 48dp so the setting remains easy to undo.

ui-tab-enters-the-group-at-the-selected-radio-or-the-first-option-if-none-is-selected-shift-t = Tab enters the group at the selected radio, or the first option if none is selected. Shift+Tab enters at the selected radio, or the last option if none is selected. Arrow keys move focus and selection between options.

ui-enter-at-the-selected-radio-or-the-first-if-none-is-selected-tab-again-leaves-the-group = Enter at the selected radio, or the first if none is selected; Tab again leaves the group

ui-enter-at-the-selected-radio-or-the-last-if-none-is-selected-move-backward-out-of-the-group = Enter at the selected radio, or the last if none is selected; move backward out of the group

